akr 0.1
project akr

record akr.papercut.bug-needs-a-decision-d-028-is-incomplete/1 : papercut {
    title "BUG (needs a decision, D-028 is incomplete): completing a COMMITTED…"
    state verified
    statement """
        BUG (needs a decision, D-028 is incomplete): completing a COMMITTED non-legacy milestone always fails akr check with AKR-R022. Proven in a throwaway repo: define milestone (commit A), add evidence, complete + commit (commit B); check then reports 'evidence predates the last content change'. Root cause: last_change_of hashes the full canonical record text (crate::hash::content_hash via canonical_hash_input, which strips only comments), so the completion itself - state proposed->completed plus the acceptance verified_by citations - counts as the newest content change, and any cited evidence necessarily predates it. D-028 waived the descendant comparison only for source { kind legacy }, so ongoing non-legacy milestone completion is structurally impossible to keep green once committed. Fix direction: compute last_change over the milestone's DEFINITIONAL content only (exclude state and acceptance verified_by, and lifecycle/provenance fields like reason), matching D-016's stated intent ('stop a test from 200 commits ago closing a milestone redefined yesterday'). Warrants a D-029 decision + tests in validate/rules.rs and git/last_change_of.
        """
    observed_at git:c3c5c4c243aa1256eee11fa43aee8ac6df62abfa
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}

record akr.papercut.calling-the-knowledge-papercut-mcp-tool/1 : papercut {
    title "Calling the knowledge.papercut MCP tool returned 'unsupported call',…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Calling the knowledge.papercut MCP tool returned 'unsupported call', even though knowledge.search and knowledge.context route fine and crates/akr-mcp/src/tools.rs wires knowledge.papercut. The installed MCP server binary predates the D-027 papercut work; it needs a rebuild/reinstall from this branch to expose the tool.
        """
    observed_at git:30579aeb4960ca7b4de2659953ce0694541bfa96
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}

record akr.papercut.cargo-fmt-check-fails-on-the-committed-tree/1 : papercut {
    title "cargo fmt --check fails on the committed tree: several files from the…"
    state verified
    statement """
        cargo fmt --check fails on the committed tree: several files from the last two commits (render/*, resolve/mod.rs, validate/rules.rs, akr-mcp record.rs/schema.rs/tools.rs, args.rs, write.rs) have formatting drift. A contributor running the documented 'cargo fmt' gets a large diff unrelated to their change, and a CI fmt gate would already be red.
        """
    observed_at git:30579aeb4960ca7b4de2659953ce0694541bfa96
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}

record akr.papercut.historical-port-design-gap-recovered-from-a/1 : papercut {
    title "Historical-port design gap, recovered from a lost agent session…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Historical-port design gap, recovered from a lost agent session (originally logged in the bpg-rs ledger as bpg.papercut.v-020-s-descendant-commit-freshness-gate-akr/1). A single-commit port of old history validated clean before commit, but once the ledger was committed akr check raised 19 AKR-R022: D-016/V-020's descendant-commit rule wants each completed record's evidence to postdate the record's last content change, which is structurally impossible for a transcription of history whose evidence commits predate the port commit. RESOLVED by D-028 (2026-08-05): a completed record carrying source { kind legacy } waives the descendant-commit comparison only (evidence must still resolve, record result pass, and be a commit the repo has). Ports like bpg-rs and the planned jp2lam go green once re-checked with a D-028 binary and their completed records carry a legacy source block.
        """
    observed_at git:047a684214734d19ebc8a477030ceb9cfbc98ceb
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}

record akr.papercut.root-cause-of-the-discoverability-miss-the-cli/1 : papercut {
    title "Root cause of the discoverability miss: the CLI's AKR-C011 error…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Root cause of the discoverability miss: the CLI's AKR-C011 error carries help 'run akr init to create one', but the MCP surface drops it — crates/akr-mcp/src/errors.rs builds its diagnostic object with only code and message (no help field), so an agent hitting C011 over MCP sees 'no .akr directory found' with no remedy. Fix: propagate EnvError.help into the MCP diagnostics payload.
        """
    observed_at git:30579aeb4960ca7b4de2659953ce0694541bfa96
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}

record akr.papercut.the-akr-mcp-knowledge-tools-failed-with-akr/1 : papercut {
    title "The akr MCP knowledge.* tools failed with AKR-C011 'no .akr directory…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The akr MCP knowledge.* tools failed with AKR-C011 'no .akr directory found' at the repo root because AKR had no root ledger of its own — the only papercut records lived inside example fixtures the MCP server could not reach. Finding recorded papercuts meant grepping the filesystem. Fixed by running akr init at the repo root (this ledger).
        """
    observed_at git:30579aeb4960ca7b4de2659953ce0694541bfa96
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}
